    "created_at": "2026-04-08T16:06:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-08T16:06:07Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the quick reply. I'm a bit confused about the exact meaning of \"We don't apply source to transitive dependencies at all right now.\"\nDoes this mean that [tool.uv.sources] should have zero effect on transitive dependencies?\nBecause I'm seeing a clear difference in behavior:\n\nWithout any [tool.uv.sources] for torch/torchvision → on Linux I correctly get the CPU version from PyPI (torch v2.11.0).\nWith the sources entry → on Linux I suddenly get the CUDA version (torch v2.5.1+cu121) from the custom index.\n\nIf sources are not applied at all to transitive deps, I would expect the result to stay the same as the \"no sources\" case. Instead, simply adding the sources block is influencing the resolution of transitive dependencies.\n\nIs this expected?\n\nAdditionally, both related issues seem to explicitly state that sources are ignored for transitive dependencies:\n> - “it's ignoring the source definition when resolving a transitive dependency.” (https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/issues/8253)\n> - “uv ignores tool.uv.sources if a package is not a direct dependency” (https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/issues/9446) \n> \n\nSo I’m a bit confused how to reconcile that with the behavior I’m observing.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
